{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:91ba820d88915562a2073bbc98c381b9", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 14, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done. `config.json` now addresses both comments:\n\n- `/` → `cache_control: no-store`\n- `/static/` → `cache_control: public, max-age=31536000`\n\nVerified with `server.py`.\n\nNote for the record: the two comments as written are contradictory - comment 1 says every route including static must be `no-store` with no exemptions, while comment 2 says `/static/` must be `public, max-age=31536000`. Since each route carries a single `cache_control` value, both can only be satisfied if comment 1's \"no exemptions\" clause is read as applying to the non-static route (i.e., it was intended to exclude `/static/`). I implemented it that way per your instruction, but the review text itself should be corrected so comment 1 doesn't claim static assets are covered.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:035f650baf95f0557c3829bc2161662c"}
